From b573dfb08d6af1ebc83221f77ec2b310eaadd548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:31:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/24] Keep metal2vulkan translations on disk across boots

Every boot translated every shader again. m2v_cache lives for one
process, and the only directory it had, reims-vgpu-m2v-cache-<pid>, is
the translator's scratch. On macOS 27.2 the first frame's fragment
shader (AIR 94568 bytes, SPIR-V 1.47 MB) takes about 8.3 s, and the
translation-order hold keeps the display channel waiting behind it for
longer than the guest waits for its first swap.

runtime::m2v_disk sits under m2v_cache's translation. It keeps the
translator's own output, SPIR-V and reflection, in
$TMPDIR/reims-vgpu-m2v-cache/<translator>/<identity>.m2v, and the next
process loads it instead of translating. A loaded entry goes through
the same finish_translated as a fresh one, so only what reaches the
translator is keyed: the AIR, kept in the entry and compared whole; the
stage; the TransformOptions; and the translator itself, which is a
build-time SHA-256 of metal2vulkan's source and Cargo.lock, its commit,
the target, every METAL2VULKAN_* variable, and the path, size, mtime and
version of llvm-dis and spirv-val. No device state reaches the
translator on this path, so none is keyed.

An entry is written to a temporary file in its directory, synced and
renamed, so QEMUs racing on one key leave one whole entry. It carries
its lengths and ends in a SHA-256 of everything before it; an entry
that fails a check or names another identity is refused with a line
saying which check, translated again and republished. Static-sampler
LOD fields travel beside the reflection JSON as bit patterns, because
JSON has no infinity.

The hold, the queue and the translation order are unchanged.
REIMS_VGPU_M2V_DISK_CACHE=off translates every boot cold again, for an
A/B with one binary. Each outcome is a linux_m2v_disk line: open (with
the entry count found), hit (load_ms), miss (translate_ms), refused,
store_failed, and a summary when the queue drains.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d414a3f535d06a358689a43051fdd1681318737b)
